# CQLite Subagents

Focused subagents for CQLite development. Each `.md` file here is one agent (its frontmatter has the
canonical `description`). **Pass an explicit `model` on spawn** — the pinned frontmatter model may be
inaccessible.

## Available Agents

| Agent | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `flow-lead` | Delivery lead/PM — drives the flow-* pipeline, sequences the specialists, never writes production code |
| `sstable-developer` | SSTable parsing/implementation, binary-format debugging, Cassandra 5 compatibility |
| `rust-reviewer` | Read-only Rust code review (Read/Glob/Grep), quality-standards enforcement |
| `test-validator` | Test execution, sstabledump parity, failure investigation |
| `spec-auditor` | Intent audit (C) — implementation vs OpenSpec change / issue acceptance criteria |
| `coverage-reviewer` | Test-quality review — whether tests are meaningful, not merely present |
| `compaction-parity-auditor` | Byte-for-byte write/compaction parity gap audit vs Apache Cassandra |

## Usage

Invoked automatically by task context, or explicitly ("use the sstable-developer agent to…"). Specialists
are sequenced by the lead via the `flow-*` pipeline (`docs/development/pm-operating-loop.md`).

## Related Skills

Skills in `.claude/skills/` provide domain knowledge (auto-loaded) and pipeline verbs:

- `sstable-parsing` · `cql-type-system` · `rust-patterns` · `rust-skills` — domain knowledge
- `ci-cd-validation` — tiered gate loop + merge-on-green
- `test-data-management` — working with test SSTables
- `flow-groom` / `flow-activate` / `flow-implement` / `flow-address` / `flow-finalize` / `flow-board` —
  the delivery pipeline (`start-epic`/`pm-status` are deprecated pointers → flow-*)
